<article class="env-lemma" id="08R3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08R3">Lemma <span data-tag="08R3">92.8.5</span>.</a> Let $A \to B \to C$ be ring maps such that $L_{C/B} = 0$. Then $L_{C/A} = L_{B/A} \otimes _ B^\mathbf {L} C$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a trivial consequence of the distinguished triangle (<a href="/tag/08QS" data-tag="08QS">92.7.0.1</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>